    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0263" n="253" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg253"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ballantine</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-03-02">March 2, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There is attached for your consideration a tentative list of topics for
                    discussion with Ambassador Hurley.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d178-f1"/> Some of
                    these topics you may wish to discuss with Mr. Hurley, especially the subject of
                    our policy toward China, and there are attached also for your reference two
                    memoranda, a short one by Mr. Vincent<anchor n="22" xml:id="d178-f2"/> dealing
                    with the question of military support to Chinese groups in areas of American
                    military operations and a longer one by Mr. Drumright<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d178-f3"/> (with contributions by Messrs. Stanton and Vincent)
                    dealing with a wider range of problems. You will of course also wish to consider
                    in this connection the contents of Mr. Atcheson’s telegram no. 324, February 28,
                    1 p.m.</p>
                <p>I assume that you will wish to delegate to us in FE the discussion of most of the
                    topics in the attached list.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">oseph</hi>] W. B[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">allantine</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
